{"title":"BFS","slug":"BFS","html":"<div class=\"wk-navbox\">\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-title\">\n<p><a data-wiki=\"File Systems\" href=\"#/library/File_Systems\">Filesystems</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Virtual Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"VFS\" href=\"#/library/VFS\">VFS</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Disk Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT\">FAT</a> <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_12\">12</a>/<a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_16\">16</a>/<a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/fat_32\">32</a>, <a data-wiki=\"FAT\" href=\"#/library/FAT/vfat\">VFAT</a>, <a data-wiki=\"ExFAT\" href=\"#/library/ExFAT\">ExFAT</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Ext2\" href=\"#/library/Ext2\">Ext 2</a>/<a data-wiki=\"Ext3\" href=\"#/library/Ext3\">3</a>/<a data-wiki=\"Ext4\" href=\"#/library/Ext4\">4</a> · <a data-wiki=\"LEAN\" href=\"#/library/LEAN\">LEAN</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HPFS\" href=\"#/library/HPFS\">HPFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"NTFS\" href=\"#/library/NTFS\">NTFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HFS\" href=\"#/library/HFS\">HFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"HFS+\" href=\"#/library/HFS_plus\">HFS+</a> · <a data-wiki=\"MFS\" href=\"#/library/MFS\">MFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ReiserFS\" href=\"#/library/ReiserFS\">ReiserFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"FFS (Amiga)\" href=\"#/library/FFS_Amiga\">FFS (Amiga)</a> · <a data-wiki=\"UFS\" href=\"#/library/UFS\">FFS (BSD)</a>/<a data-wiki=\"UFS\" href=\"#/library/UFS\">UFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"BeFS\" href=\"#/library/BeFS\">BeFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"BFS\" href=\"#/library/BFS\">BFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"XFS\" href=\"#/library/XFS\">XFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"SFS\" href=\"#/library/SFS\">SFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ZDSFS\" href=\"#/library/ZDSFS\">ZDSFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"ZFS\" href=\"#/library/ZFS\">ZFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"USTAR\" href=\"#/library/USTAR\">USTAR</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">CD/DVD Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"ISO 9660\" href=\"#/library/ISO_9660\">ISO 9660</a> · <a data-wiki=\"Joliet\" href=\"#/library/Joliet\">Joliet</a> · <a data-wiki=\"UDF\" href=\"#/library/UDF\">UDF</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\"><a href=\"#/library?cat=Network_Filesystems\">Network Filesystems</a></span> <a data-wiki=\"NFS\" href=\"#/library/NFS\">NFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"RFS\" href=\"#/library/RFS\">RFS</a> · <a data-wiki=\"AFS\" href=\"#/library/AFS\">AFS</a></p>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-navbox-row\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-navbox-group\">Flash Filesystems</span> <a data-wiki=\"JFFS2\" href=\"#/library/JFFS2\">JFFS2</a> · <a data-wiki=\"YAFFS\" href=\"#/library/YAFFS\">YAFFS</a></p>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"wk-note wk-stub\">\n<p><span class=\"wk-note-label\">Stub</span></p>\n<p>This page on the OSDev Wiki is a stub: it covers the basics but is not complete.</p>\n</div>\n<h2 id=\"about_bfs\">About BFS</h2>\n<p><strong>BFS</strong> (<strong>UnixWare Boot File System</strong>) is a SCO specification for a KISS <a data-wiki=\"File Systems\" href=\"#/library/File_Systems\">filesystem</a> used at <a data-wiki=\"Bootloader\" href=\"#/library/Bootloader\">bootstrap</a>. It only offers one directory and, due to the way information about blocks are stored, only one file opened for writing at a time.</p>\n<dl>\n<dt></dt>\n<dd>\n<em>From what i see, it also means BFS will have to do nasty things if a file must be extended after some other file has been created</em> -- PypeClicker\r\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl>\n<dt></dt>\n<dd>\n<em>Agreed, but it's not a general-purpose filesystem. One tends not to extend things like the kernel image or modules.</em> -- Strib\r\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<dl>\n<dt></dt>\n<dd>\n<em>What about updates? Also, why aren't we using the discussion page instead?</em> --<a class=\"ext wk-missing\" href=\"https://wiki.osdev.org/User:Love4boobies\" rel=\"noopener\">Love4boobies</a> 12:06, 7 January 2011 (UTC)\r\n</dd>\n</dl>\n<h2 id=\"see_also\">See Also</h2>\n<h3 id=\"external_links\">External Links</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><a class=\"ext\" href=\"http://www.penguin.cz/~mhi/fs/bfs/bfs-structure.html\" rel=\"noopener\">The BFS filesystem structure</a></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"about_bfs","text":"About BFS","level":2},{"id":"see_also","text":"See Also","level":2},{"id":"external_links","text":"External Links","level":3}],"categories":["Filesystems"],"rating":null,"flags":["stub"],"words":219,"summary":"BFS ( UnixWare Boot File System ) is a SCO specification for a KISS filesystem used at bootstrap . It only offers one directory and, due to the way information about blocks are stored, only one file opened for writing…","updated":"2011-01-07","authors":["Love4boobies"],"url":"https://wiki.osdev.org/BFS","history":"https://wiki.osdev.org/index.php?title=BFS&action=history","backlinks":[{"t":"AFS","s":"AFS"},{"t":"BeFS","s":"BeFS"},{"t":"ExFAT","s":"ExFAT"},{"t":"Ext2","s":"Ext2"},{"t":"Ext3","s":"Ext3"},{"t":"Ext4","s":"Ext4"},{"t":"FAT","s":"FAT"},{"t":"FFS (Amiga)","s":"FFS_Amiga"},{"t":"File Systems","s":"File_Systems"},{"t":"HFS","s":"HFS"},{"t":"HFS+","s":"HFS_plus"},{"t":"HPFS","s":"HPFS"},{"t":"ISO 9660","s":"ISO_9660"},{"t":"Initrd","s":"Initrd"},{"t":"JFFS2","s":"JFFS2"},{"t":"Joliet","s":"Joliet"},{"t":"LEAN","s":"LEAN"},{"t":"MFS","s":"MFS"},{"t":"Modular Kernel","s":"Modular_Kernel"},{"t":"NFS","s":"NFS"},{"t":"NTFS","s":"NTFS"},{"t":"RFS","s":"RFS"},{"t":"ReiserFS","s":"ReiserFS"},{"t":"SFS","s":"SFS"},{"t":"Symbolic link","s":"Symbolic_link"},{"t":"UDF","s":"UDF"},{"t":"UFS","s":"UFS"},{"t":"USTAR","s":"USTAR"},{"t":"VFS","s":"VFS"},{"t":"XFS","s":"XFS"},{"t":"YAFFS","s":"YAFFS"},{"t":"ZDSFS","s":"ZDSFS"},{"t":"ZFS","s":"ZFS"}],"lessons":[]}